From ecf5664fd3a03b69fedddde3b265b0c4f6168606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FP mod <fpmod@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:22:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/27] Mystery encounters: a ? holds one of the floor's rarer
 enemy groups

When a floor is built, each party that will show as a ? is swapped for a set
from that floor's own table that the floor lists less often (counted over all
its layouts' spawn picks), weighted toward the rarest; never a boss set, and
one already the rarest stays. The party and its map model are filled in as the
game fills a new one. F1 checkbox, setting mystery_rare (on by default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1oHeiADE8njqFxkaQnJAX
